notes: V0311 adds a persistent Junction Network workspace on top of the existing intersection topology and multi-camera foundations. Each junction can own one or more source_ids, one optional primary_source_id and a persisted canvas position, while each source remains exclusive to one junction so live source identity is unambiguous. The new /api/traffic/network/overview projection combines configured nodes/links, saved ESP camera health, current shared-pipeline vehicle/pedestrian load, ranked-scenario/service/test events and warnings for visualization. Only the junction resolved from the current selected camera/simulation source receives live AI/simulation traffic metrics; V0311 explicitly does not claim simultaneous multi-junction inference or physical/public-road control. The frontend Junction Network page supports draggable nodes, directed links, junction add/remove/edit, multi-camera assignment/reassignment, primary-camera selection and live event/warning badges. V0310 camera transport behavior remains unchanged. V024 / 0_2_4 remains the owner-confirmed passed baseline until explicit owner acceptance changes it.
